{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01N6Nx634zm1QmxRbRKSe9QR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All ten SOS cards are implemented, tested, and committed. The full suite passes: **1242 tests** (1145 engine regression + FDN reference + 53 new SOS card tests), with zero regressions and a clean working tree.\n\n**What was built:**\n\n*Shared engine seams (E1–E3, one commit):*\n- E1: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` now fires from `cast_spell` *and* `cast_spell_free` (free casts are still \"cast\" per rule 601; copies correctly never fire it).\n- E2: new `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` fired from `GameState.advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()`.\n- E3: `get_cost_reduction` aggregates `spell_cost_reduction` from the caster's battlefield permanents for instants/sorceries.\n\n*Ten cards, one commit each, in build order:* sos_4 (Converge), sos_1 (graveyard cost reduction + free cast on attack + exile-instead), sos_245 (affinity self + grant), sos_226 (Casualty 1 with retargetable copies), sos_257 (land with restricted mana + in-place animation), sos_57 (counter + delayed colorless), sos_120 (Paradigm recurring copy from exile), sos_13 (preparation card per rule 722), sos_201 (granted miracle + opponent-upkeep loot), sos_97 (planeswalker: surveil/discard/reanimate/coin-flip skip-turns).\n\n**Notable spec-driven deviations from the plan** (all logged in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`):\n- `AttacksTriggeredEvent` existed but combat never fired it — added a per-attacker fire in `declare_attackers_step` (sos_1 needed the real path).\n- \"Exile instead\" for spells required a `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` consulted on stack exits — `move_to_zone` previously only checked replacements when leaving the battlefield.\n- sos_13's ETB lives in `on_resolve` (the fdn_157 pattern) because the engine fires ETB events before registering the entering card's own triggers; and per rule 722.3c the prepared Swords copy costs {W} — the rulebook overrode the TODO's \"cast free\" suggestion.\n- The zero-toughness SBA gained a creature-type gate (rule 704.5f) so the un-animated Great Hall isn't binned.\n- Restricted mana is a separate pool inside `ManaPool` with an optional `spell=` param on `can_pay`/`pay` — honored at payment time, additive for all existing callers.\n\nEach card was verified twice: through its committed `tests.py`, plus an independent throwaway smoke check asserting spec-observable outcomes (zones, life, P/T, exile-vs-graveyard, turn skipping) that the committed tests didn't cover."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":267134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e89db2fe-0d6e-4510-b5e6-a7586e7fc62b","uuid":"fa34df96-0371-4a47-90af-02c79f8eba28","request_id":"req_011CbwBpLc8qYz5bVXSALVfR"}
